  // became the whole channel the moment the sky went to smoke-white. What a ray
  // that leaves the surface at two degrees actually strikes is the far bank: dark
  // spruce wall and shadowed till, which is why the reference photograph's far
  // channel measures a dark olive (98,104,89) under a sky of (221,226,226).
