  // (ua - time*speed) is not a translation of the field, it is a SHEAR of it, at
  // du/dx * time / cellSize cells per metre across. Twelve seconds in that is already
  // 9-12 cells per metre and it grows without bound for as long as the session runs.
  // Any feature cut from that coordinate is combed into a channel-parallel sliver,
  // which is exactly the 8-9:1 comet at one shared angle the critic measured three
  // times. Round 7 replaced the noise with a cell field and kept the sheared
  // coordinate, so the shape changed and the streak did not.
  //
